\title{qrcmNP: Nonlinear and Penalized Quantile Regression Coefficients Modeling}
\description{
Quantile regression coefficients modeling (QRCM, Frumento and Bottai, 2016)
describes the regression coefficients \eqn{\beta(p)} of a quantile
regression model as parametric functions of the quantile order \eqn{p}, and
estimates all quantiles simultaneously by minimizing an integrated loss
function. 'qrcmNP' extends this framework in two directions:
}
\details{
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=piqr]{piqr()}}: penalized QRCM for covariate selection (Sottile et al., 2020),
with lasso and group lasso penalties, tuning by AIC/BIC (\code{\link[=gof.piqr]{gof.piqr()}}) or
cross-validation (\code{\link[=cv_piqr]{cv_piqr()}}), and post-selection inference
(\code{\link[=refit_piqr]{refit_piqr()}});
\item \code{\link[=niqr]{niqr()}}: nonlinear parametric quantile models, in which the quantile
function can be a nonlinear function of the parameters, of the covariates,
or both (Bottai and Cilluffo, 2020), with sandwich, cluster-robust and
bootstrap standard errors, information criteria (\code{\link[=gof.niqr]{gof.niqr()}}) and a
goodness-of-fit test (\code{\link[=test.fit.niqr]{test.fit.niqr()}}).
}
}
